        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "195c3fc2-dcbf-5a68-a0b5-260e389ad190",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Okinawa, Operation Iceberg, Operation Diadem, Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino, Battle of the Liri Valley\n- Places: Okinawa, Monte Cassino, Liri Valley, Italy\n- Organizations: United States Marine Corps, United States Army, Imperial Japanese Army, U.S. Fifth Army, British Eighth Army, Allies of World War II\n- Topics: Pacific War, World War II, Italian Campaign of World War II, amphibious assault\n\nFacts:\n- In May 1944, Operation Diadem was an Allied offensive in the Italian Campaign of World War II undertaken by the U.S. Fifth Army and the British Eighth Army.\n- Operation Diadem was also referred to as the Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino and, in Canada, the Battle of the Liri Valley.\n- On April 1, 1945, the Battle of Okinawa began with the invasion of Okinawa.\n- The Battle of Okinawa, codenamed Operation Iceberg, was a major battle of the Pacific War fought on Okinawa by United States Marine and Army forces against the Imperial Japanese Army.\n- The invasion of Okinawa included the largest amphibious assault in the Pacific War during World War II.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
